# A .crx let go on chrome://extensions with developer mode on installs it, as in Chrome and Arc: the page asks
# chrome.developerPrivate for the file being dropped, Chrome shows its "Add extension?" prompt over the window, and
# Add installs it (GitHub #593). Dropped.crx is self-signed (no Web Store proof), which the page's drop allows.
# A package Chrome refuses (DroppedCrx2.crx, the old CRX2 format) says why in Chrome's bar over the page instead
# of doing nothing. A real drag from another app's window took the same path on 0.1.49, 0.1.52 and main.
# promise: #593
budget rss=600
cra://open?url=chrome://extensions/
wait 3
cra://debug?pageJS=chrome.developerPrivate.updateProfileConfiguration({inDeveloperMode:true})
wait 1
cra://debug?dropFile=${FIXTURES}/DroppedCrx2.crx
expect-log dropFile: entered=.* performed=true
expect-log info bars: Package is invalid: 'CRX_HEADER_INVALID'
cra://debug?dropFile=${FIXTURES}/Dropped.crx
expect-log Chromium dialog [0-9]+ shown over window
# Chrome enables Add a moment after the prompt shows.
wait 1
cra://debug?chromiumDialogs=Add extension
expect-log Chromium dialogs: frame=\{\{.*\}\} over=\{\{.*\}\} onScreen=true titleBarHidden=true
expect-log Chromium dialog pressed Add extension
wait 3
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"chrome.developerPrivate.getExtensionsInfo().then(l=>JSON.stringify(l.map(e=>[e.name,e.state])))","awaitPromise":true}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*Cra Dropped CRX.*ENABLED
